    "narrative": "For August 20th, our offensive strategy for Ghost Ride the WHIP hinges on capitalizing on favorable matchups against mid-tier arms. **Isaac Paredes** (66.57) and **Brice Turang** (63.14) headline our daily efficiency ratings. **Isaac Paredes** benefits significantly from a projected #3 spot in the order and a favorable platoon advantage against Grayson Rodriguez, providing a high floor for counting stats. **Brice Turang** remains our engine for stolen base production; despite a projected leadoff role against Kirby, the matchup remains playable, and his projected 10% boost from the leadoff spot makes him a primary anchor for the day. **Max Muncy** (62.02) also projects well, capitalizing on a strong matchup against Dobnak where his power profile aligns perfectly with the SP skill volatility.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's docket was excluding **Vinnie Pasquantino** (48.79) from the starting 1B/UTIL slots. While **Vinnie Pasquantino** offers reliable contact, the combination of a tough lefty matchup against Jump and the sheer density of our current starters\u2019 order-based boosts tipped the scales in favor of **Austin Riley** and **Josh Naylor**. We are also keeping a close eye on **Jose Caballero** (57.99); while he possesses the requisite elite sprint speed we covet, the projection is dragged down by a low-leverage #9 spot in the order. Owners should be wary of lineup volatility, as both **Brice Turang** and **Isaac Paredes** remain pending; if their respective managers slide them down the order, we may see a decline in their overall production efficiency. Finally, our bench remains depleted by the absences of **James Wood** and **Mickey Moniak**, meaning we have little room for error if any of our starters are late scratches.",
